00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
How did I do this? I can’t explain it. 

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:19.000
How do billions of tiny birds cross the world’s largest desert, every year, without food or water?

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:26.000
When humans look at our route on a map, they realise that that no sane creature would cross it. 

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:31.000
It is insane, when you think about it. 

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.000
So we do not think. There is no space in our bodies for thoughts. 

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:45.000
All the energy goes to the flight. Because our bodies know that, no matter how dangerous that journey is, what we leave behind is worse. 

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:53.000
And we want to live. So we fly.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:59.000
I flew non-stop for fifty hours. Two full days and two full nights. 

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:04.000
The night air was freezing cold, the daytime sun scorching hot. 

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:12.000
There were thousands, millions of us in the air, all moving in the same direction, racing on the most dangerous highway. 

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.000
Yet, during the crossing, we were alone. 

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:28.000
I crossed like I was in a dream, the adrenaline pumping through my veins, making my wings move as if they were not my own, giving me a strength I didn’t know I had. 

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:34.000
I couldn’t feel the pain, the hunger, the cold, the exhaustion. 

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:43.000
“You’re almost there”, my ancestors whispered. 

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:49.000
My mom told me it was like hatching eggs. You don’t know how you do it, nature shows you how. 

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:58.000
You just do it, and then you forget. Nobody wants to remember the pain, otherwise you wouldn’t have the strength to do it again.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:04.000
And then, I made it to the other side. 

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:10.000
There may have been an oasis. Or a city. I don’t remember any of it.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:15.000
I simply remember that I landed somewhere and I passed out. 

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:22.000
But in my dreams, I knew I was safe.  
